{"availability":"available","full":"jcerrell-IS/can-it-ford","name":"can-it-ford","description":"Can a specific vehicle ford a flooded road? A three-level model ladder from depth thresholds to coupled MPM water and rigid-vehicle simulation on TACC GH200/A100, with every claim traced to its source. NSF SCIPE REU 2026, GeoElements Lab, UT Austin.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-21T06:51:06Z","updated":"2026-10-13T11:48:30Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://can-it-ford.vercel.app","topics":["civil-engineering","computational-fluid-dynamics","flood-modeling","gaussian-splatting","gpu-computing","gradio","hpc","huggingface","material-point-method","nsf-reu","python","reproducible-research","scientific-computing","simulation","tacc","vehicle-stability"],"demo":"https://can-it-ford.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:05.321Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:05.321Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:05.321Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:34:36.222Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T19:48:56.569Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T03:00:05.321Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Can a specific vehicle cross a specific flooded road? Three models answer, from a one-line depth rule to a coupled GPU water simulation, and the interesting result is where they disagree.","WARPMPM simulation on TACC Lonestar6 (job 3484188): a Toyota Yaris hull held fixed, broadside, in a 20 m wide periodic channel of water 0.30 m deep moving at a mean 1.0 m/s, 30 s after the flow started. Each dot is a simulated water particle in the upper half of the water, coloured by speed. The run did not pass the project's pre-registered steadiness test, so the image shows a flow pattern, not a measured drag.","This is a research project, not a safety tool. Its thresholds come from draft and interim criteria for stati